Subject: SDCP key derivation (only needed when OpenSSL < 3.2, no change on newer versions)

Applied by install.sh to the libfprint-egismoc-sdcp source before building,
only while the source still needs it (it is skipped once the source has the
fix). Remove this file when the fix is in the fork.

fpi_sdcp_kdf() passes host_random and device_random as two separate
OSSL_KDF_PARAM_INFO parameters. OpenSSL 3.2+ KBKDF joins repeated INFO values
(ossl_param_get1_concat_octet_string), but OpenSSL 3.0 and 3.1 only read the
first (OSSL_PARAM_locate_const), so device_random is silently dropped, the
master secret is wrong and "SDCP ConnectResponse claim validation failed"
every time. Affects distros with OpenSSL 3.0/3.1, e.g. Ubuntu 24.04 and its
derivatives (Linux Mint 22, Zorin 17/18, Pop!_OS 24.04) and Debian 12
(MX Linux 23). Seen on issue #1 of abdallah-alkanani/libfprint-egismoc-sdcp.

Joining them into one INFO value gives the same bytes OpenSSL 3.2+ produces,
so nothing changes where it already worked. libfprint's own known-answer test
/sdcp/key_derivation fails on OpenSSL 3.0.13 without this and passes with it.

diff --git a/libfprint/fpi-sdcp.c b/libfprint/fpi-sdcp.c
index a3bbc17..653a38b 100644
--- a/libfprint/fpi-sdcp.c
+++ b/libfprint/fpi-sdcp.c
@@ -631,6 +631,7 @@ fpi_sdcp_kdf (GBytes      *key,
   g_autoptr(EVP_KDF) kdf = NULL;
   g_autoptr(EVP_KDF_CTX) kdf_ctx = NULL;
   g_autofree guint8 *secret = NULL;
+  g_autoptr(GByteArray) context = NULL;
   OSSL_PARAM params[8];
   int i = 0;
 
@@ -650,15 +651,27 @@ fpi_sdcp_kdf (GBytes      *key,
                                                    (void *) label,
                                                    strlen (label));
 
-  if (context_a)
-    params[i++] = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string (OSSL_KDF_PARAM_INFO,
-                                                     (void *) (g_bytes_get_data (context_a, NULL)),
-                                                     g_bytes_get_size (context_a));
-
-  if (context_b)
-    params[i++] = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string (OSSL_KDF_PARAM_INFO,
-                                                     (void *) (g_bytes_get_data (context_b, NULL)),
-                                                     g_bytes_get_size (context_b));
+  /* Pass the context as ONE info parameter (context_a || context_b).
+   * OpenSSL 3.2+ joins several OSSL_KDF_PARAM_INFO values itself, but
+   * OpenSSL 3.0/3.1 KBKDF only reads the first one, which silently drops
+   * context_b (device_random) and gives a wrong master secret — the SDCP
+   * Connect MAC then never matches. Joining them here gives the same bytes
+   * as OpenSSL 3.2+ does, on every OpenSSL 3 version. */
+  if (context_a || context_b)
+    {
+      context = g_byte_array_new ();
+      if (context_a)
+        g_byte_array_append (context,
+                             g_bytes_get_data (context_a, NULL),
+                             g_bytes_get_size (context_a));
+      if (context_b)
+        g_byte_array_append (context,
+                             g_bytes_get_data (context_b, NULL),
+                             g_bytes_get_size (context_b));
+      params[i++] = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string (OSSL_KDF_PARAM_INFO,
+                                                       context->data,
+                                                       context->len);
+    }
 
   params[i++] = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end ();
 
